# SERVESTOCK - REQUIREMENTS & RUNNING COMMANDS (KEYS)

---

## 📋 System Requirements

| Requirement | Minimum Version | Description |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Node.js** | `v18.0.0` or higher | JavaScript runtime environment |
| **npm** | `v9.0.0` or higher | Package manager bundled with Node.js |
| **MongoDB** | `v6.0` or higher | Database (Local server on `mongodb://localhost:27017` or Atlas cluster) |
| **Git** | `v2.0` or higher | Version control system |
| **Expo Go App** | Latest | Mobile testing app (Download from Android Play Store / iOS App Store) |
| **Android ADB** *(Optional)* | `android-tools-adb` | Required for USB debugging on Android devices |

---

## ⚙️ Initial Project Setup Commands

Run these setup commands after cloning the repository:

```bash
# 1. Clone Repository
git clone https://github.com/ARIPRAKASH32/ServeStock.git servestock
cd servestock

# 2. Install Dependencies
cd backend && npm install && cd ..
cd frontend && npm install && cd ..
cd mobile && npm install && cd ..

# 3. Create Backend Environment File (.env)
echo "PORT=5000" > backend/.env
echo "MONGODB_URI=mongodb://localhost:27017/servestock" >> backend/.env
echo "JWT_SECRET=your_super_secret_jwt_key_here" >> backend/.env
echo "JWT_EXPIRES_IN=7d" >> backend/.env
```

---

## 🚀 Running Commands

### 1. From Project Root Directory (`/home/ariprakash/Documents/ServeStock`)

| Command | Action |
| :--- | :--- |
| `npm run dev` | Starts Web Frontend (Vite server) |
| `npm run dev:frontend` | Starts Web Frontend (Vite server) |
| `npm run dev:backend` | Starts Backend Server (Nodemon + Express API on port 5000) |
| `npm run start:mobile` | Starts Mobile App (Expo Dev Server) |

---

### 2. From Specific Subdirectories

#### 🌐 Web Frontend (`/frontend`)
```bash
cd frontend
npm run dev      # Starts Vite dev server (http://localhost:5173)
npm run build    # Builds production bundle
npm run preview  # Previews production build locally
```

#### ⚙️ Backend API (`/backend`)
```bash
cd backend
npm run dev      # Starts development server with hot-reload (http://localhost:5000)
npm run build    # Compiles TypeScript to JavaScript in /dist
npm start        # Runs production build from /dist
npm test         # Runs Jest test suite
```

#### 📱 Mobile App (`/mobile`)
```bash
cd mobile
npx expo start   # Starts Expo Metro Bundler server
npm run android  # Launches directly on Android target
npm run ios      # Launches directly on iOS target
npm run web      # Launches Expo web app preview
```

---

## ⌨️ Expo Terminal Keyboard Shortcuts (Interactive Keys)

When running the mobile app server (`npm run start:mobile` or `npx expo start`), use these keypresses:

| Key | Action |
| :--- | :--- |
| `c` | Display QR Code to scan with Expo Go app |
| `a` | Open app on connected Android device / emulator |
| `w` | Open app preview in Web browser |
| `r` | Reload the mobile application |
| `j` | Open React Native Debugger |
| `m` | Toggle Developer Menu on connected device |
| `Shift + m` | Open additional Expo tools |
| `Ctrl + C` | Stop the Expo development server |

